meta:
  origin:
    producer: Velasco
    title: LGBTI National Policy Dataset
    description: |-
      The LGBTI National Policy Dataset (Version 2.0) is a country-year-policy panel tracking the adoption, scope, and enforcement of LGBTI-related policies across 196 countries from 1991 to 2025. The dataset is distributed in long format: each row records one country in one year for one specific policy-status combination. It is designed for use in comparative political research, policy diffusion analysis, and quantitative cross-national studies of LGBTI rights.

      The dataset covers 27 distinct policy areas organized into 54 policy-status combinations (each policy paired with two mutually exclusive status directions). Of these 54 combinations, 37 contain substantive data; the remaining 17 are structural placeholders with all-zero values, included to maintain a fully balanced panel suitable for econometric methods.
    citation_full: |-
      Velasco, Kristopher. 2026. "LGBTI National Policy Dataset, Version 2.0." Distributed via Open Science Framework: osf.io/wta9p.
    attribution_short: Velasco
    version_producer: '2.0'
    url_main: https://osf.io/wta9p/overview
    # Stable OSF GUID link for LGBTI_Policy_Data_Long.csv — resolves to the file's latest version.
    url_download: https://osf.io/download/zpd78/
    date_accessed: '2026-07-15'
    # NOTE: The producer replaced the data file and codebook on OSF on 2026-06-12 (6,813 changed
    # Proportion cells vs the 2026-03-23 release) while keeping the "Version 2.0" label — the
    # version_producer field can't distinguish revisions; compare file dates on OSF when updating.
    date_published: '2026-06-12'
    # NOTE: The OSF project declares no license (verified 2026-07-15, and in the April 2026 Wayback
    # capture) and the producer's site states none, so the earlier "CC BY 4.0" claim was unsupported.
    # Producer copyright is the conservative default until Velasco confirms terms — update on reply.
    license:
